{"c":[{"id":"5b436031a992daa5","sum":"Ask's sentences: planner/says.ts, sent as error.says. Pin setGeneratorClock offline. Jev Choice confidence = top-two margin. Intent writer: 8k tok/min, space evals 30 s. Unrouted producers self-trigger; routed hold offers (routing.idle). B27 memory sets: evidence/screen/b27.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"78eeba3d0e4f7ab9","sum":"Ask's sentences live in planner/says.ts (SaidError message, sent as error.says since H5); pin setGeneratorClock in offline measurements. Jev Choice confidence is the top-two margin (0.75 floor ~0.875 winner). Intent writer gpt-oss-120b: 8k tokens/min, space Ask evals 30 s.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"943dffc1dbc84f96","sum":"B26: Ask's sentences live in planner/says.ts; a SaidError's message is what the user reads (since H5 sent as error.says), its detail holds the check's text. Offline generator measurements must pin setGeneratorClock or cold first forms are cut short.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T224111Z-32ca3d0fc6e98438","text":"B26: every Ask refusal or question sentence lives in planner/says.ts; a SaidError's message is what the user reads and its detail holds the check's text (ids, provider errors). Scoreboards print both.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T224111Z-6a820f7b64075f54","text":"B26: offline generator measurements (scripts/realfill-budgets.ts and the like) must pin setGeneratorClock, or cold first forms are cut short by the time budget and the numbers vary run to run.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"47481f5f6fb24ec8","sum":"D2-02: Jev Choice confidence is the margin between the top two option probabilities (a 0.75 floor needs ~0.875 on the winner). Groq gpt-oss-120b, the Ask intent writer, allows 8,000 tokens/min; intents are ~2,000, so Ask evals space calls 30 s or get 429.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233505Z-310484d235184787","text":"D2-02: Jev Choice 'confidence' is the margin between the top two option probabilities (raw answers also carry 'probabilities'); a 0.75 floor needs about 0.875 on the winner.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T233506Z-254786afcaf981c8","text":"D2-02: Groq gpt-oss-120b (the Ask intent writer) allows 8,000 tokens a minute; an intent is about 2,000, so Ask evals space calls 30 s or get 429 'unavailable'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1f86caa19701c852","sum":"D2-02: without HelperOptions.routing producers self-trigger; routed producers hold offers (await routing.idle() then routedSettled). Duplicate naps after a merge go at the next note. B27: score B17/B18 memory sets with the relabelled copies in evidence/screen/b27/memsets.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"94b9c96f4bec8c25","sum":"D2-02: without HelperOptions.routing producers self-trigger (tests, evals); main.ts routes when Jev is on; routed producers hold offers, so await routing.idle() then routedSettled. I4: a merge of two branches that napped the same notes lists them twice until a note refolds.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233521Z-ca79b84757c7cc74","text":"D2-02: HelperOptions.routing absent keeps producers self-triggering (tests, producer evals); main.ts routes when Jev is on. Routed producers hold offers (engine.release/dropHeld, openApp.showHeld, events.judge); await routing.idle() then routedSettled.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T233858Z-3b9ba7299adc0299","text":"I4: when two merged branches each napped the same notes, git keeps both naps and wake lists their lines twice (T2's 60b138f0/b105c8e9 vs H4's 7234fe4d); summem has no command to drop one, so fold before branching or accept the duplicate.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c7e9161a825c4d83","sum":"I4: after a merge with duplicate naps, the next summem note refolds and drops them; write a note and do its naps. B27: B17/B18 memory held-out sets label own First/Last name 'none'; score with the relabelled copies in evidence/screen/b27/memsets.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T234020Z-7134731208a83f08","text":"I4 correction: the next summem note after such a merge re-plans the folds and drops the duplicate naps (one copy left per line, checked with recall); just write a note and do the naps it asks for.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T235441Z-17480ff5b594d902","text":"B27: B17/B18 memory held-out sets label the user's own First/Last name fields 'none' (written when fill copied values only whole); score them with the relabelled copies in ~/.caret-run/evidence/screen/b27/memsets, whose about-fill-eval accepts expect first/last.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"dab2f5b7a08bdf02","sum":"U2: Not right is a click on the slip's source row; stand-ins clip; debug JSON omits nil; the perch is a rim drawn only while uncovered. D2-02: diff Router 1 per moment. B27: failed fills reach users via Helper.fillFailed. B28: await site.waitForLoad; use fake-app.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c8d5b05b4e63693d","sum":"U2: Not right on an offer is a click on the slip's source row (keyboard: the fact's row in What Caret knows); stand-ins must clip; debug JSON omits nil keys (.get()); the perch is a rim on the task's window, drawn only while uncovered.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"a6b54378f08f606c","sum":"U2: Not right on an offer is a click on the slip's source row only (NotRightTarget); its keyboard path is the fact's row in What Caret knows. Off-screen stand-ins (ScrollingColumn) must take the height offered and clip, or the knows window's footer falls out of renders.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T000002Z-0878a22fa544c193","text":"U2: Not right on an offer is a click on the slip's source row only (NotRightTarget, a tiny click panel over that row); no key is claimed, and the keyboard path is the fact's row in What Caret knows.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T000002Z-0ab9ad748298511d","text":"U2: SwiftUI's off-screen stand-ins (ScrollingColumn) must take the height offered and clip, as a GeometryReader does; a fixed-size stack in a flexible frame pushed the knows window's footer out of renders.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"52b95150f4d0fe88","sum":"U2: debug JSON omits nil keys (read with .get()); the perch is a rim, perch and caption on the task's own window, drawn only while Rim.seen says it is uncovered; corner perch and perch-avoid are gone.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T000002Z-69ceb492909786b0","text":"U2: the host's debug JSON leaves out nil keys (synthesized Codable), so a script must read them with .get(); memory_documents_walk.py misread a closed editor as still open.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T000002Z-b1b1695c4d5b6282","text":"U2: the perch is now a rim, perch and caption on the task's own window, drawn only while Rim.seen says nothing covers it; the corner perch, PerchPlacement and perch-avoid are gone (perch-avoid now answers with an error).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"49622ae7d74e40f9","sum":"D2-02: Router 1 flips near its 0.5 floor between runs, so diff per moment before crediting a recall move. B27: failed fills reach users only via Helper.fillFailed. B28: wait for site.waitForLoad after navigation; accept.ts cannot run executor.run (use fake-app.ts).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ccba801a8aa9c8ea","sum":"D2-02: Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of its 0.5 floor flip between corpus runs; diff per moment before crediting a recall move. B27: a failed fill reaches the user only via Helper.fillFailed (planner/says.ts fillSays); ids go to warn.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T031924Z-459c6ef9ec89ae5d","text":"D2-02: Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of its 0.5 floor flip between live corpus runs (m02 0.52/0.49, m09 0.45/0.51); diff runs per moment before crediting a code change with a recall move.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T032639Z-5905894b0fafbfcc","text":"B27: a failed fill reaches the user only through Helper.fillFailed (planner/says.ts fillSays); its window and field ids go to warn. Early exits that called this.error published ids until afadd34.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"91fb33162eeab888","sum":"B28: after a fixture page navigates, wait for site.waitForLoad before the next site.command; accept.ts cannot run executor.run (watchInput gets noWindow), so test page-link VerbResults there and the executor with test/fake-app.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T044215Z-74ca06dede7d18b3","text":"B28: after a fixture page navigates away, wait for site.waitForLoad of the landed page before the next site.command, or the command goes to the departing page's long poll and times out.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T044215Z-8ef7ae66324e8796","text":"B28: accept.ts cannot run executor.run: it first asks the native reader for watchInput and gets noWindow; check page-link VerbResults in accept and the executor with test/fake-app.ts knobs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
